    "chunk_text": "1AIV (w) jeks fldgi \u2014 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'09'17Part IV(A) \u2014 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 17.09.2025\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2454$37 - 2025 iema;e\u00efn\u00be ui 17 jeks nodod - 2025'09'17No. 2454/37 - WEDNESDAY, SEPTEMBER 17, 2025\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART IV (A) \u2014 PROVINCIAL COUNCILS\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nSABARAGAMUWA PROVINCE PROVINCIAL COUNCIL\n\nSecond Supplementary Financial Statement 2025\n\nGRANTING PERMISSION BY VIRTUE OF POWERS VESTED IN ME UNDER SECTION 27 (A) OF PROVINCIAL COUNCIL ACT NO. 42 OF 1987 AS THE TERM OF THE SABARAGAMUWA PROVINCIAL COUNCIL OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA ENDED ON 26TH SEPTEMBER, 2017.2025\n\n1. This permission may be cited as \u201cPermission to disburse under the Second supplementary financial statement - 2025 of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council\u201d and come in to operation from 30.07.2025.\n\n2. The expenditure of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council which is estimated Rupees Sixty Two Billion Two Hundred Eight Million Fifty-five Thousand Eighty Two and Twelve Cents only (Rs. 62,208,055,082.12) for the service of the period beginning on 01st of January, 2025 and ending 31st December, 2025, which is specified as \u201cFinancial Year 2025\u201d in the Annual Financial Statement and Revenue and Expenditure Estimate for 2025 approvd on 03.04.2025, as amended by the First Supplementary Estimate for 2025 is hereby amended as, Rupees Sixty Two Billion Five Hundred Twenty Two Million Five Hundred Seventy Eight Thousand Seven Hundred Thirty Nine and Forty Five Cents only (Rs. 62,522,578,739.45) and grant permission to the Chief Secretary of this Province and other Accounting Officers to disburse the same from the Sabaragamuwa Provincial council Fund."
