    "chunk_text": "PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA.\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2455$14 - 2025 iema;e\u00efn\u00be ui 23 jeks w`.yrejdod - 2025.09.23No. 2455/14 - TUESDAY, SEPTEMBER 23, 2025\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERALGovernment Notifications\n\n1A - PG 7259 - 05 (09/2025) This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nPUBLIC UTILITIES COMMISSION OF SRI LANKA\n\nEstimated expenditure for the Year 2026\n\nTHE Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka was established under the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka Act, No. 35 of 2002. In accordance with the requirements stipulated under Sections 33(2) and 33(3) of the said Act, the Commission is required to publish the estimated expenditure for the following year in the Government Gazette. Accordingly, the Commission approved budget for 2026 is forwarded herewith.\n\n1. Electricity Sector Rs. 781, 991,853\n\nOutcome 1. Increase the affordability of electricity Rs. 165,884,207 2. Ensure Reasonable Electricity Charges Rs. 64,201,686 3. Improve the efficiency of the electricity industry Rs. 118,298,971 4. Improve the convenience of consumers Rs. 65,019,013 5. Improved safety for life and property Rs. 117,517,410 6. Enhanced Electric Vehicle charging infrastructure Rs. 50,880,225 7. Enhance Renewable Energy integration to achieve 70% Renewable Energy target Rs. 95,090,157 8. Corporate reports and information dissemination Rs. 105,100,184\n\n2. Petroleum Sector Rs. 69,185,599\n\nTotal Budget Rs. 851,177,452\n\nProf. K. P. L. Chandralal, Chairman, Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka. EOG 09 - 0217"
