    "chunk_size_bytes": 1639,
    "chunk_text": "(c) the driver or owner of a dual-purpose vehicle, light motor coach, motor coach or heavy motor coach engaged in daily office transport service or school transport service and driven or used on or entered into an expressway which has not been fitted by the manufacturer with individual safety seats belt as specified in regulation 8E for the rear centre seats or several rear seats at the time of coming into operation of regulations 8 A, 8B and 8C.\n\n(2) The provisions of regulations 8A, 8B and 8C shall not apply to-\n\n(a) children under the age of twelve years and persons whose height does not exceed 135 centimeters;\n\n(e) passengers travelling in an emergency service vehicle.\n\n8E. The type of the individual safety seat belt that is required to be fitted in every motor vehicle to which regulations 8A, 8B and 8c apply shall be as follows: -\n\n(a) the driver\u2019s seat belt shall be a standard seat belt comprising three anchor points, consisting of a strap running upwards and strap running laterally across the body; and\n\n(b) seat belts for other seats including the seats in the front row shall be a standard seat belt comprising of a strap running laterally across the body with at least two anchor points, depending on the design of the seats.\n\n8F. Save as provided in sub-regulation (2) of regulation 8D, the provisions of Motor Traffic (Seat Belts) Regulations, No. 3 of 2011 published in Gazette Extraordinary No. 1718/12 of August 09, 2011 shall not apply to the driver or owner of the motor vehicles driven or used or enter in to an expressway.\u201d.\n\nEOG 09 - 0239\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
